lation') showing that dialect-specific behavioral features (turn length, repair frequency) in AAVE vs. SAE agentic dialogues exhibit variance that is NOT explained by the generic demographic prompt. If SCOPE's 1.5% variance figure comes from survey data (not agentic task-completion), this rebuttal may be straightforward.\n\nWith these fixes, the paper could plausibly target EMNLP 2026 Findings or SIGDIAL 2026 as primary venues rather than EMNLP Main.",
